State parity: refuges everywhere, no phantom layers

An audit of what each state actually carried turned up a real gap: federal
refuge hunt units were built for New Hampshire only. Massachusetts has 56,
including Monomoy with a 3,224 acre waterfowl hunt area and the Parker
River hunting areas. Refuges are now core rather than an NH extra.

Layer toggles are filtered by whether the shown states carry the data, so
no state sees a switch that does nothing. Strings that named one state are
gone: the outside-a-zone message, the tide hint, the refuge heading, and
the Sunday note, which now names whichever states actually close Sundays.

Regs, Sources gains a coverage table so it is visible what each state has
and what it does not publish. Base map, wind, location, habitat, the hunt
log and every tool behave the same in every state - the only differences
are datasets a state does not publish.

